   "source": [
    "- The previous scores of the students indicates the wide variation between 50 and 100, suggesting that most students scored 50 and higher and the distribution of score is roughly uniform.\n",
    "- The exam score, on the other hand, has right-skewed disribution. The histogram shows that most students have exam scores concentrated between 60 and 75, while a smaller number achieve very high score near 80-100, which raises the mean above the median. \n",
    "- Moreover, students who had lower previous scores appear to have improved, showing higher performance in this exam, while those who previously had high scores tend to perform slightly lower this time. This may suggest a convergence in performance, where weaker students catch up and stronger students drop slightly.\n",
    "- Overall, the data indicates that exam performance is fairly consistent across students, with no large spread or extreme variation, with more students performing in the middle to higher range, and fewer achieving top marks."
   ]
