   "source": [
    "The scatter plot shows a slight upward trend between attendance and exam scores, indicating that students who attend class more frequently tend to achieve somewhat higher scores. However, the relationship is not very strong — some students with lower attendance still manage to achieve top marks, while others with high attendance do not necessarily score the highest. This suggests that while consistent attendance may contribute to better performance, it is not the only factor influencing exam results. Other variables, such as study habits, motivation, or access to resources, might play a larger role in determining student outcomes."
