  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3197c417",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Although the dataset already includes several academic, behavioral, and socioeconomic vairables, it remains cross-sectional and does not capture changes over time. To strengthen the analysis, I would collect longitudinal data that tracks students’ study hours, attendance, and scores across multiple semesters. More information collected about study techniques, mental health, course difficulty, and teacher effectiveness,... would also be helpful to isolate the impact of study time. Including such data would make the model more credible by accounting for omited factors. These variables could be obtained through school surveys, student feedback systems, or instituitional academic databses."
   ]
